<PageLayout title="Review Methodology" description="How Sublime Pantry compares freeze dryers and gear: stated criteria, documented specifications, and honest labels for what we have and haven't tested." path="/review-methodology">
  <span class="kicker">Policy</span>
  <h1>Review methodology</h1>
  <h2>The honest starting point</h2>
  <p>We are building our own testing program, and until a product has been through it we will not pretend otherwise. Every comparison on this site carries a methodology box stating whether it is a <strong>specification comparison</strong> (built from manufacturer documentation and expert sources) or a <strong>bench-tested review</strong> (built from our own measurements). Today, all comparisons are specification comparisons.</p>
  <h2>How specification comparisons work</h2>
  <p>Criteria are declared before products are compared — typically price, batch capacity, tray area, power requirements, pump type, warranty, and service considerations. Figures come from manufacturer pages and documentation, cited with access dates. Where manufacturers disagree with third-party listings, we use the manufacturer's own figure and note the discrepancy. Prices are listed with the date checked, because they change.</p>
  <h2>What a future bench test will include</h2>
  <p>When our testing program launches, each machine test will publish its protocol: identical loads by weight and food type, logged cycle times, energy metering, finished-product water-activity readings, and noise measurements — along with sample size and limitations. Tests will be reproducible by any reader with the same equipment.</p>
  <h2>Conflicts</h2>
  <p>We hold no affiliate relationships today. If we add them, or ever sell our own product in a category we compare, that relationship will be disclosed inside the comparison itself — see our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
